hen $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{5,6,7,…,37\\},$ and the set $S=\\{5,6,7,…,37\\}$ has $|S|=37-5+1=33$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{33}, & x=5,6,7,…,37 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=10)=f(10)=\\frac{1}{33}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16667a3e-7935-543d-862c-a62e273500bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588393} {:answer/id #uuid "8539983f-a86a-539d-a6d8-49bf55e7593c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588628} {:answer/id #uuid "95708a8f-ba96-567d-923a-71c62f3d695d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588666} {:answer/id #uuid "cf66c48c-3a52-51de-92a9-f7fc03ef5e5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588781} {:answer/id #uuid "cf904eb0-c58b-53a7-8c31-b03db8dc2757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588782}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588628} :answer-field/id #uuid "531a3eb6-3ba9-5a00-861e-e24b730f0d01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ccb2214-989d-5e9c-8a76-84733f2c7931" :question/math-academy-id "q-164159" :question/problem "Given that $X∼U\\{-10,-9,-8,…,5\\},$ compute $P(X=5).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{-10,-9,-8,…,5\\},$ and the set $S=\\{-10,-9,-8,…,5\\}$ has $|S|=5-(-10)+1=16$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}, & x=-10,-9,-8,…,5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=5)=f(5)=\\frac{1}{16}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d828d263-b2a1-5ecb-b762-412c0d3ba821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588796}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588796} :answer-field/id #uuid "42c2596b-06fd-520f-9298-a98db7ebad4a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588910} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76c893e3-646d-52a8-8e75-6971f8fe44d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588598}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588598} :answer-field/id #uuid "5425ef84-d355-5da6-8986-9bc443985b51" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dacad8a7-b4aa-5de2-bb78-a7a0cf3529e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2-x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588803} :answer-field/id #uuid "961606e9-0909-584e-a439-a5f4b6c606f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "976d95e8-05cc-5ef9-90ff-d659b5653cea" :question/math-academy-id "q-275742" :question/problem "A stick of length $2$ is broken at a point chosen uniformly at random along its length. Let the continuous random variable $X$ denote the distance from the left end of the stick to the break point, and let $Y=Y(X)$ denote the length of the longest piece.\n\nExpressing the integrands in the following equation as polynomials, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\text{E}[Y]={\\int }_{0}^{1}\n$$\n{{field-1}} $$\n\\displaystyle \\text{d}x\\,\\,+\\,\\,{\\int }_{1}^{2}\n$$\n{{field-2}} $\\text{d}x$\n\nTherefore, the expected length of the longer piece is  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ and a function $r(x)$, the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(x)]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\text{ }\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x)$ is the probability density function of $X.$ \n\nIn this problem, the break point $X$ is chosen uniformly from $[0,2]$, so the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\le x<2.\n$$\n\nWhen the stick is broken at point $X$, it is divided into two pieces: one of length $X$ and the other of length $2-X.$ The longer of the two pieces, $Y$, is therefore given by\n\n$$\nY=\\text{max}(X,2-X).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we define\n\n$$\nr(x)=\\text{max}(x,2-x).\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the integral, we express $r(x)$ as an explicit piecewise function. Observe that,\n\n- if $0\\le x\\le 1$, then $x\\le 2-x$, so the longer piece has length $2-x$,\n\n- if $1<x\\le 2$, then $x>2-x$, so the longer piece has length $x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nr(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2-x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ x, & 1<x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & =\\text{E}[\\text{max}(X,2-X)] \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[2x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-\\frac{1}{2})+\\frac{1}{2}(2-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the expected length of the longer piece is $\\frac{3}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589099 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c304cc-2f1e-5591-924c-65aea8f54d11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588351} {:answer/id #uuid "5a38a3e4-6ce0-5817-846c-224fe448994d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588524} {:answer/id #uuid "80549c91-d57c-533c-a185-2ff29ff85ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588616} {:answer/id #uuid "8c258306-8c3f-5f7f-b2c5-fb609d4a97cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588647} {:answer/id #uuid "adbbe4df-1761-5512-91ff-d85ca9764359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588716}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588716} :answer-field/id #uuid "60d85d67-d5e5-5fac-b491-6d07207a97bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a4133711-c595-5d9a-ae06-76103ab567dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-96808" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{4,5,8,9,10,12,13\\},$ compute $P(X\\ge 5).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{4,5,8,9,10,12,13\\},$ and the set $S=\\{4,5,8,9,10,12,13\\}$ has $|S|=7$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7}, & x=4,5,8,9,10,12,13 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $6$ items $(5,8,9,10,12,13)$ that satisfy $X\\ge 5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 5)=6\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}=\\frac{6}{7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589102 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c1b6525-dfed-5b33-87b7-e9d66bbc8979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588470} {:answer/id #uuid "7e28c342-a073-549f-b694-878ede6ddd53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588614} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7869ca-929c-56d5-9dd9-22cd6af5ff71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588642} {:answer/id #uuid "b6991d84-07ee-5c2f-87d3-e894f3a2e323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588734} {:answer/id #uuid "bea84b04-e3b4-5203-999e-e544a131f46e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588749}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588470} :answer-field/id #uuid "815e0376-ce42-5300-a36f-11a2f46b8e3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "aca44ccc-621c-5c00-8b6c-6886203a07b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-96777" :question/problem "Given that $X∼U\\{5,6,7,8,9,10\\},$ compute $P(X=8).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{5,6,7,8,9,10\\},$ and the set $S=\\{5,6,7,8,9,10\\}$ has $|S|=6$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}, & x=5,6,7,8,9,10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=8)=f(8)=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "482d036e-0c7d-53f7-bfa5-6b3445120118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588493} {:answer/id #uuid "4d780bcc-ac20-5b6c-b692-6e09181835ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588501} {:answer/id #uuid "5a7666bc-b551-5240-adba-e264a1405f7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588526} {:answer/id #uuid "8db27c4d-1648-5754-b9a4-1041d29746a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588651} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a7428b-e768-509f-8851-d92c08597525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588501} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5d7f84d-7c37-5faf-abe1-1b51962feb20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b670f2b5-5794-53cc-9361-ced9725c804c" :question/math-academy-id "q-164163" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\\},$ compute $P(2<X\\le 7).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\\},$ and the set $S=\\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\\}$ has $|S|=9$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}, & x=0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $5$ items $(3,4,5,6,7)$ that satisfy $2<X\\le 7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(2<X\\le 7)=5\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{5}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5976bf14-7973-5f04-ad0f-c27cc95b6715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{e}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588522} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3894ba-bc95-5f34-90c6-2595f1fa02f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588584} {:answer/id #uuid "97639a6a-56d0-5233-ab30-508d2119a74d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588670} {:answer/id #uuid "cafd346e-7b26-51a4-96b0-4b11f90e921d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{e}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588773} {:answer/id #uuid "cc8d9b08-3f83-58a9-96e7-deebe5c76eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588774}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588522} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7a16cfd-be20-56b4-a812-7c47e535bca8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c3883a23-c34b-572b-8ae0-05d8a0406877" :question/math-academy-id "q-137161" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{e}^{-3X}],$ given that the continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x+1}, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nr(x)={e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{e}^{-3X}] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x}\\cdot {e}^{-x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}[{e}^{-4x+1}]_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(0-{e}^{-3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "295b54ff-0b52-5d84-bdc0-cf7ffd790cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588429} {:answer/id #uuid "385bec9d-dd85-5008-bccf-27eb2c98f298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588462} {:answer/id #uuid "5f918f53-29c9-53b7-97aa-97711797b71f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588539} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2f957c-7486-5cce-aba4-ef3e85a2791d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588710} {:answer/id #uuid "e8bdf5cc-84e6-5b5f-9bfd-f3deefc929c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588833}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588539} :answer-field/id #uuid "dea3f739-2726-550a-95c1-3ff13bff7641" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ee7045b1-191e-55c1-8803-1b2990ac2aa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-96809" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{5,9,12,13,14,15\\},$ compute $P(X<12).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{5,9,12,13,14,15\\},$ and the set $S=\\{5,9,12,13,14,15\\}$ has $|S|=6$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}, & x=5,9,12,13,14,15 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $2$ items $(5,9)$ that satisfy $X<12.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X<12)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12d0e505-4d06-5574-ba13-34d366edf31c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588384} {:answer/id #uuid "134183cf-8d3c-5b7f-8fe1-57344c3613d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588387} {:answer/id #uuid "35e5d0cc-28b6-531a-90bf-2dfe991534d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588457} {:answer/id #uuid "5d974122-ad88-5896-b449-58878146917f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588533} {:answer/id #uuid "5df4eea5-8899-56a7-b570-07e4dd4273e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186588534}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186588533} :answer-field/id #uuid "d75bbb96-2f8f-59fd-b884-70370b33e129" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ff6b6360-cd10-5857-98fc-8ab04c27d2a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-137064" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[\\frac{1}{X}],$ given that the continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4x{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nr(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\frac{1}{X}] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot 4x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2[{e}^{-2x}]_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-2(0-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ff886bd-48a6-57d4-8137-bcd5f1509a24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}+\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589271} {:answer/id #uuid "360ca67f-e35a-5aca-a2a7-f1e18a75911b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589367} {:answer/id #uuid "685d5392-7949-5f02-a5de-08819bf5ff02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589476} {:answer/id #uuid "98f368b8-c08c-5e92-a7e9-c5001cd7366c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589579} {:answer/id #uuid "9e576fc5-b53c-52cc-ae39-12ea62f585d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi (\\pi +8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589592}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589579} :answer-field/id #uuid "9804be92-56c1-561c-824f-5e01afc642e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "137128f7-1a14-5a28-951a-e1696681e4ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-143886" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[Y+1],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=y+1.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $$\n\\displaystyle D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y+1] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}(y+1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+1)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{4}{\\pi }(y+1){\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{4}{\\pi }(y+1)[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{4}{\\pi }(y+1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+y]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{32}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f40236-4a19-51ac-bfae-d9ed17517a88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589239} {:answer/id #uuid "1d23cdb9-4012-5d3c-9c6f-a43094a465c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589305} {:answer/id #uuid "43d32329-7ff1-5155-b193-1cc0287fafb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589404} {:answer/id #uuid "e85d188b-082e-5c9c-b385-4ebb8af44d95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589742} {:answer/id #uuid "f9dfe403-03d4-5ff4-b525-3133b7f91c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589783}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589239} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b8a7ebf-6029-5f14-969c-7a08ed57562a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "172af9cf-cf87-5ef5-ba5b-d020852d17a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130690" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{9}{2}],$ compute $P(X\\ge 1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{9}{2}],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & \\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{9}{2}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 1) & =P(1\\le X\\le \\frac{9}{2}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{9/2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{9/2}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{9}{2}-1)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e35ab3d-3ecf-548c-8dba-3664929a1f26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589310} {:answer/id #uuid "30e61243-3e65-5ebf-ab2d-ac055a57d459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589354} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8c77a6-9e46-5943-9cc5-a1c451d13d57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589519} {:answer/id #uuid "e926968c-c607-53cd-baca-9cd9ea931e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589747} {:answer/id #uuid "f39951ac-d2a2-59fa-ad53-d17484a3df4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589768}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589768} :answer-field/id #uuid "44a5ca76-f376-5e07-ab3b-7d21ac705a3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1c399478-c0bc-5f36-bf4d-9746f1dff23a" :question/math-academy-id "q-143883" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[X+Y],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=x+y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X+Y] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}(x+y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\cdot 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3x{y}^{2}+3{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}}{2}+3x{y}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}+3{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{3{y}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf735cc-3713-561d-9047-bc69e28e8caa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589302} {:answer/id #uuid "22678666-e168-5ce6-8355-0937b51d505e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589321} {:answer/id #uuid "6453eee5-92fc-5fdd-a71f-586088a96966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589473} {:answer/id #uuid "acc6b7cd-3362-5985-a6f2-7ca62907c69f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589618} {:answer/id #uuid "bc403710-df0d-54f0-95ef-40100322166f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589648}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589618} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba137976-dfd9-5a12-b8b5-8e5c81a1c9fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1f39b8f1-50f1-5719-9acb-5c74bacc2013" :question/math-academy-id "q-96331" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $V$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\frac{1}{2},2],$ compute $P(-1\\le V<\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $V$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(v)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le v\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $V$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\frac{1}{2},2],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(v)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}, & -\\frac{1}{2}\\le v\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1\\le V<\\frac{1}{2}) & =P(-\\frac{1}{2}\\le V<\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}f(v)\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}-\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}{\\frac{5}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aab8de5-2778-582c-af2c-66a55c028ffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589253} {:answer/id #uuid "12f77a2d-156f-5690-9b5a-1ec0ffc1b66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589275} {:answer/id #uuid "31960911-a6b7-57af-a641-a7ae997c08b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589355} {:answer/id #uuid "51297f33-5ed2-5baa-8833-42aff64ed568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589430} {:answer/id #uuid "a82a7c08-7299-5fa6-856c-69be9ba6cddf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589608}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589430} :answer-field/id #uuid "36b61323-fbf5-5f75-8e9b-f4989a748690" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "21d26b28-4182-52a2-8360-5cb5df01b9c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-110984" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}cy,\\, & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{4}{3},\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le 2-y, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $$\n\\displaystyle D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{4}{3},\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le 2-y\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/2c/2c984b3c51548a6c9181575cefe27427d12f07c499c4b44fd3fd0bddb0d710af.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{4/3}{\\int }_{y/2}^{2-y}cy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating  $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4/3}[{\\int }_{y/2}^{2-y}cy\\,dx]dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{4/3}[cxy]_{x=y/2}^{x=2-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4/3}(cy(2-y)-c\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4/3}(2cy-\\frac{3c{y}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4/3}(2cy-\\frac{3c{y}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y & ={[c{y}^{2}-\\frac{c{y}^{3}}{2}]}_{0}^{4/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16c}{27}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{16c}{27}=1\\,⇒\\,c=\\frac{27}{16}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0275cfaf-e6f0-5113-ae3c-1e3917010b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589232} {:answer/id #uuid "4487a470-8e80-5a2e-96de-2baf9233696b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589406} {:answer/id #uuid "91e9b3f0-46e7-5a6e-bb92-f297a902c1ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589562} {:answer/id #uuid "993f0e04-091f-55e0-9dcc-90a9da4c6dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589581} {:answer/id #uuid "d9cac3fa-1232-58e1-a36b-e09e0be7441b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589717}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589562} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ee1d3ee-2671-55e2-8b4e-b4fb2a7990ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "298fc742-1a5d-5a1e-b95d-7bb702e20086" :question/math-academy-id "q-143882" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}+2Y],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)={x}^{2}+2y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonzero only in the rectangular region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X{Y}^{2}] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}({x}^{2}+2y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+2y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+2y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+xy]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{4}{3}+2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[\\frac{4}{3}y+{y}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f7c32e-a688-5e33-861c-1af2cca08757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589240} {:answer/id #uuid "3b4c76d8-dc39-5f61-8d86-917267ec4eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589386} {:answer/id #uuid "aabc4020-8599-59d0-aecc-d47608832b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589613} {:answer/id #uuid "b6767d50-e08a-5f14-84e1-27a9094145f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589638} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f2350b-89fa-5e4e-b1c6-30fbd8b4a6af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589672}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589613} :answer-field/id #uuid "3002f8ad-fc52-5f76-b627-a707aa223a50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2ba64a4a-7680-5cfe-8c61-9bd52700ec5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-110860" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}c{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\n\n![](images/f6/f60587953ec9bbe05689382b641677058ce8ba070917db340a0ba793170d0951.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}c{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}c{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{c{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9c{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9c{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =[3c{x}^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n3c=1\\,⇒\\,c=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a3f84e-d01b-572d-8f1d-3439a8e16ab9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589541} {:answer/id #uuid "925f2d26-8acb-55d1-8d9e-0934e1ecab61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589564} {:answer/id #uuid "b6467070-9b4c-5436-94ba-7ec4e6be2974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589637} {:answer/id #uuid "d1124ea4-e0cc-5fdc-92a4-a9f2f51005c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589698} {:answer/id #uuid "f242b372-fa02-516b-89db-6f131f26cfb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589764}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589764} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f9ab8a3-51be-5acf-88ac-d2b1a4af1009" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "33b66d8b-f78d-530b-b4b4-d6685a5f4324" :question/math-academy-id "q-130544" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[k,11k],$ where $k$ is a positive number, compute $P(0<X<6k).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[k,11k],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10k},\\, & k\\le x\\le 11k, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X<6k) & =P(k<X<6k) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{k}^{6k}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{k}^{6k}\\frac{1}{10k}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6k-k}{10k} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e8ced3e-c319-5503-970d-62c53b0ec9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589391} {:answer/id #uuid "761c6467-ff46-5946-a30a-a683a6f52a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589508} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ffaa7c-eddb-5612-a8f3-1ee5f31ede02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589660} {:answer/id #uuid "d3571ef0-2a65-51a5-b252-2490e3a2d51c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589704} {:answer/id #uuid "edad270d-e751-5c82-b77d-1c8d8c9f1efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589752}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589391} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8c44b53-f021-5c1e-87be-47c2b9e8fea8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "37c4266b-f3f4-5336-97ec-391af6105b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110988" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{{y}^{2}},\\, & 1\\le x\\le {y}^{3}\\le 8, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le {y}^{3}\\le 8\\}.$\n\n![](images/ec/ecf0160f62333198c74110695da7f1800836f20a5d646e436df2520ddd1acfe6.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{3}}\\frac{c}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating  $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{3}}\\frac{c}{{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{c}{{y}^{2}}[x]_{x=1}^{x={y}^{3}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{c}{{y}^{2}}({y}^{3}-1)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(cy-\\frac{c}{{y}^{2}})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(cy-\\frac{c}{{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{c{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{c}{y}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(2c+\\frac{c}{2})-(\\frac{c}{2}+c) \\\\  & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c72170-0185-58da-a3b1-1781e02b26ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589326} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe74922-70d6-5411-9e1e-1000ccf0bb22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589394} {:answer/id #uuid "48ff37ee-b04f-5038-aad4-b6c0268d4966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589414} {:answer/id #uuid "6e83cca1-3f96-51c2-bb38-7cffeafffd08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589491} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba9392e-0f5b-5ba7-ac89-4e1480b7d272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589522}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589394} :answer-field/id #uuid "24846375-d795-5bc7-846f-4fc7736fb988" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3d702ca2-c6ae-50e6-92b6-a2af4a2e7c27" :question/math-academy-id "q-111164" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y<2X-2{X}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,1]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A=\\{Y<2X-2{X}^{2}\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](images/bb/bb3b94fbd5ae245b60fbd496be1a4609742bb1958148faeae57ca3ef4054f6da.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<2X-2{X}^{2}) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x-2{x}^{2}}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x-2{x}^{2}}4xy\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[2x{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=2x-2{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2x(2x-2{x}^{2})^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(8{x}^{3}-16{x}^{4}+8{x}^{5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{4}-\\frac{16{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{4{x}^{6}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{16}{5}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a88c861-9e1e-540b-aa38-13c5670aa663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589380} {:answer/id #uuid "45b7faea-b0bc-564e-b020-7966512436d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589410} {:answer/id #uuid "a591d94c-f16b-506f-8250-c7804460e58c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589604} {:answer/id #uuid "d9051c8a-646f-5201-ae98-2a9f24bd7117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589714} {:answer/id #uuid "e45a1102-c921-5380-9563-f4bd9fa3cb7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589735}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589714} :answer-field/id #uuid "194723e8-c5a4-5ed9-bbd0-ffdffb0c953d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4d7f1892-38c3-511f-be79-316ec2a6f9bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-130689" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,11],$ compute $P(W\\ge 7).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,11],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8},\\, & 3\\le w\\le 11, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\ge 7) & =P(7\\le W\\le 11) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{7}^{11}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{7}^{11}\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{11-7}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e26e93-7c70-52f6-819b-42ea303a3cf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589336} {:answer/id #uuid "5b699ccb-af7b-5d77-b6dc-8e387107730d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589450} {:answer/id #uuid "61e2e68b-0402-55b0-8ba9-1dc72598335d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589467} {:answer/id #uuid "74985f9a-fa74-51ab-ab7c-cad40f250d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589504} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a866d1-342b-5164-8f89-782101bda3a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589713}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589467} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fcf9b96-c377-5796-8729-bd3ca6f5c26d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "533b180e-3df5-5413-a28f-8a98a7e03303" :question/math-academy-id "q-130543" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,5],$ compute $P(X\\le 3).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,5],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(0\\le X\\le 3) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3-0}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590010 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2045be9b-c844-5f1c-a424-d19a51096189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589315} {:answer/id #uuid "70cf5757-f58c-51ca-8588-69f9b2e7983c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589497} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba7d56e-2d51-5e72-a036-8949888fecff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589521} {:answer/id #uuid "955eb754-f2a1-5b14-a5e9-d310e01dbe5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589572} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4abc83-954f-5513-b61b-45d86a25b054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589790}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589790} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8a46903-df81-580f-ae2a-583e0fd7b93a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "558378ec-8147-5add-ba23-c65cf284fb6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130548" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-7,3],$ compute $P(-5<X\\le 1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-7,3],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10},\\, & -7\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-5<X\\le 1) & ={\\int }_{-5}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5}^{1}\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-5)}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a6896c7-c04f-580b-ba46-d9b1b1cc1538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589379} {:answer/id #uuid "49158edc-ea35-5644-bf91-5340faadd93c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589415} {:answer/id #uuid "9a71bc26-7b81-59cc-8e61-e9d269072107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589585} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f5bc1c-07b4-5e54-a289-075e947875e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589784} {:answer/id #uuid "ff52983f-6138-5374-990c-8cb08f86c395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589800}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589784} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd7edde-b0c1-5c98-b6e2-56f1461876a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5842d5e5-05c8-57b2-b6ae-282181c942e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130546" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,12],$ compute $P(-1\\le X\\le 3).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,12],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 12, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1\\le X\\le 3) & =P(0\\le X\\le 3) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3-0}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590018 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a81b273-12c1-5d36-92f3-2b257559fc6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$h$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589448} {:answer/id #uuid "6cff4f17-b430-5b3f-94d6-f1c6b8a5d702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589488} {:answer/id #uuid "92c21586-4091-53f1-a00f-739aa10f1ff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$g$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589566} {:answer/id #uuid "b28a66df-34e0-5715-9305-13295df060bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f$ and $h$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589629} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b4992a-1f26-5d39-9e4c-403000822a40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f$ and $g$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589710}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589566} :answer-field/id #uuid "479cfc87-ec79-5a8d-9896-0347be5501c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6b17b395-2c2e-5267-abb7-bce287999d6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-110863" :question/problem "Let $D=[1,2]\\times [0,2].$ Which of the following functions are valid joint probability density functions?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2-xy,\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle g(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{8},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle h(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+2y}{8},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1\n$$\n\nLet's check the above conditions for each of the given functions.\n\n- The function $f$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the first condition. For example,\n\n$$\nf(2,2)=2-2\\cdot 2=-2≱0.\\,\\times\n$$\n\n- The function $g$ is a valid probability density function. Indeed, we have $g(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}g(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}g(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2x+y}{8}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2x+y}{8}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}+xy}{8}]}_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{y+3}{8}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+3y]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h$  is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the second condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{x+2y}{8}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{x+2y}{8}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2xy]}_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{8}(2y+\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[{y}^{2}+\\frac{3y}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8} \\\\  & \\ne 1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$g$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b03caa-8103-5270-85f2-3540d6b4ce42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589247} {:answer/id #uuid "60b39e85-c8f1-5939-ba92-95402812d460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589463} {:answer/id #uuid "78219fef-4cb8-5662-bca1-001b302a28c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589513} {:answer/id #uuid "fcfe1f71-a92a-532c-a2dd-8d3a9eeae499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589793} {:answer/id #uuid "fe34dde0-5911-5c25-a781-622e6b513be9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589796}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589793} :answer-field/id #uuid "c47bdfec-a511-58b5-87c7-299a58ac7514" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "718ee1be-6238-5b0d-a1aa-d37ef0e776d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-143904" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[\\frac{1}{X}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{5},\\, & 2-y\\le x\\le \\frac{y+4}{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 2; \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2-y\\le x\\le \\frac{y+4}{2}\\},$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero.\n\n![](images/9d/9dce6bf320cb848a36da0592645c0aca40b3c310a5f1394d8f7a0423ddd0ede6.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{x}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2-y}^{(y+4)/2}\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{x}{5}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2-y}^{(y+4)/2}\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[x]_{x=2-y}^{x=(y+4)/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{y+4}{2}-(2-y))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194624a1-4f88-5669-9211-0d506debc795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3h}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589290} {:answer/id #uuid "4034b14f-3677-5124-b71e-918d83d50a22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589395} {:answer/id #uuid "4d36d266-0ca0-5fe8-8672-7da94e42fbcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589425} {:answer/id #uuid "4fdfcb9c-32e2-557a-ad1b-76a693720802" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589427} {:answer/id #uuid "e65ec2fa-5d47-5ab4-87e6-ddcbc1428050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{h}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589741}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589395} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9842dbd-b369-5abf-9b7c-9977504ee4cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "777903a4-85af-5b6f-9859-f27a3992347c" :question/math-academy-id "q-96336" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-h,5h],$ where $h$ is a positive number, compute $P(0<X\\le 3h).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-h,5h],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6h},\\, & -h\\le x\\le 5h, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 3h) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3h}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3h}\\frac{1}{6h}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3h-0}{6h} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "095afe8f-3843-5199-8933-8b8abe77a03f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589251} {:answer/id #uuid "0ade859f-de94-5f84-9a48-68ff1482073b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589254} {:answer/id #uuid "0d4a9d3d-f61d-580f-8cf4-818826847ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589259} {:answer/id #uuid "b369bc7d-fc77-5678-98b0-0bc16b89d52b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589632} {:answer/id #uuid "d6ab777c-7b62-58f3-899e-8724cb30d654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589254} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd9b6c19-06c8-5c28-9564-26e0865127af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "87e23ceb-bf50-5a20-a3dd-a84bcc7eedee" :question/math-academy-id "q-130540" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-5,-2],$ compute $P(X<-4).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-5,-2],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3},\\, & -5\\le x\\le -2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-4) & =P(-5\\le X<-4) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-4}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-(-5)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1df286bb-38fc-58d1-9c7c-92683897ab5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589307} {:answer/id #uuid "3236dfd7-2aa4-5ba4-972f-95ccee1034f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589356} {:answer/id #uuid "6b56e8a7-3a55-55ad-9616-c012891bee59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589486} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce9d81a-f628-543e-b138-f30000a3b5ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589555} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b7d04b-ac44-5bdd-9993-1fb149c46c85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589701}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589486} :answer-field/id #uuid "386d7b78-b52f-5ff6-b86f-0c04dab996f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "934d0f90-9b2f-52e8-aaba-f2f142ea6149" :question/math-academy-id "q-130691" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{7}{3}],$ compute $P(X>1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{7}{3}],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & \\frac{1}{3}\\le x\\le \\frac{7}{3}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & =P(1<X\\le \\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{7/3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{7/3}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{3}-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f1490d5-86d2-5030-87c6-b60a740bc98b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589268} {:answer/id #uuid "3419f68d-5b70-5e5f-b304-abe6d89ae323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589363} {:answer/id #uuid "34ea0de7-8010-52cb-a7d1-3bc4eeba81cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589364} {:answer/id #uuid "78d07ed6-1637-5138-b789-8b8dc9c4aac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589514} {:answer/id #uuid "853a7ff9-c5f1-51ed-b754-8bbc86713f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589537}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589514} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e103f0-2ae1-53e1-9ebd-70eac667109c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f6cf757-45d1-510d-925d-060efc7c8790" :question/math-academy-id "q-146182" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & \\,x=1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}, & \\,x=3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+3\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4be826-1692-529b-a4f9-243369bc2f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589267} {:answer/id #uuid "387c3fa8-5943-563c-bf85-0b33633b7c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589373} {:answer/id #uuid "c847fdb0-14fc-5580-9825-abfa95e17fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589676} {:answer/id #uuid "c913f483-0620-5b0e-a869-782183534863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589679} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf76486-1c7b-5073-b2ac-81a1498d9b72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589689}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589689} :answer-field/id #uuid "c92e84b9-067d-5800-8f43-30067071046e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a39d260c-4974-5b74-b3f4-08eee6a03208" :question/math-academy-id "q-96281" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $V$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-2,0],$ compute $P(V\\le -\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $V$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(v)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le v\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $V$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-2,0],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(v)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & -2\\le v\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V\\le -\\frac{1}{2}) & =P(-2\\le V\\le -\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1/2}f(v)\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{1}{2}-(-2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04dde756-d3cb-5b12-b2e8-19a55ecbec4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589238} {:answer/id #uuid "5bddb1b9-4044-5bf9-a050-b260ca4ca2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589453} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8dcae3-c38a-593f-a7d8-8b12b3dd6212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589483} {:answer/id #uuid "9956c7fe-7952-5ec3-b4ca-8979086d4fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589582} {:answer/id #uuid "ce613482-5956-5313-bf7a-c9e80cfa04f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589691}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589483} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8183c5b-6091-5078-832b-834e33f394d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d4373777-4c0c-5185-ac6a-65ddd60853a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-96294" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ compute $P(U\\ge 0).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $U$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le u\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & -\\frac{5}{2}\\le u\\le \\frac{3}{2}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U\\ge 0) & =P(0\\le U\\le \\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2}-0)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4154106d-ff01-5ce5-821a-6ab59f244526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589398} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9d3e7d-9409-5357-9d2e-87769ffa212d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589493} {:answer/id #uuid "8891af16-9a0c-52dc-9fd3-7002acb38f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589544} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae26c6c-27c5-5b87-91b4-dbf989a728b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589548} {:answer/id #uuid "9aae324f-9e8b-50bf-8b7a-2eb50789b9f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589586}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589548} :answer-field/id #uuid "fca82219-9297-52ca-adc0-2955bb84a9f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f037d7df-ebc1-5173-841d-2662ff41eae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-143863" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[\\frac{XY}{3}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-3x; \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability density function. If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={∬}_{{R}^{2}}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=\\frac{xy}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-3x\\},$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero.\n\n![](images/b5/b5a9355f0c2a39a1da71f3132c1eb3d7c72464af62b23f8a26d76df306bf9773.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\frac{XY}{3}] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}\\frac{xy}{3}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{xy}{3}\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x}\\frac{xy}{3}\\cdot 2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=3-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(3-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =3[\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "848c7a13-dbfb-5041-a74c-75500c8b3bef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589534} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff5d011-113e-5e19-8a74-6abdb7e3f48f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589558} {:answer/id #uuid "986e4a1c-b5b5-51ea-9dd7-e5d12951d9f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589576} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ffbda4-1ecb-56a6-bf5c-471ccd0df0cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589745} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f95022-2473-56c7-beb4-b339c4ca69a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589782}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589745} :answer-field/id #uuid "907787c7-6367-5897-a516-f38d7ab9fe24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fb541831-9b3a-5fd7-8e37-b74e4a193596" :question/math-academy-id "q-146193" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{6}, & \\,y=2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}, & \\,y=4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=4]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=4] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590078 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19320835-9a45-55e6-a00a-53fdbefbc7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589289} {:answer/id #uuid "2b2dd721-06fa-5888-b332-ea19bef0641f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589341} {:answer/id #uuid "b9cdee57-6749-5a2a-ac5b-b3f81e283df4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589643} {:answer/id #uuid "c7016267-fccb-5da2-b87d-6cd07e440ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589673} {:answer/id #uuid "e2602d27-c46d-5e7c-a7c5-d4fdce7161da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589730}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186589730} :answer-field/id #uuid "a67221f6-fb73-5b09-9336-ce2d59da7bd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186589910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fff8694e-6759-5587-9bc4-103657c55516" :question/math-academy-id "q-130539" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-4,0],$ compute $P(X<-\\sqrt{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-4,0],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & -4\\le x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-\\sqrt{2}) & =P(-4\\le X<-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-\\sqrt{2}}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}-(-4)}{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02cda1c9-b0ce-53f9-90ec-4c01349fc2d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0431" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590191} {:answer/id #uuid "1ae8c91d-3349-5934-b917-6de5f140d8f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0331" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590222} {:answer/id #uuid "46a67834-8ee1-5cfb-be9b-6156ecd5eec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3431" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590315} {:answer/id #uuid "7d58385b-e4f2-5f8e-b4d2-c877af5ed2e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0411" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590394} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a805ce-4a88-5e52-972a-04239ff27c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1431" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590526}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590191} :answer-field/id #uuid "4532f29e-b252-5467-b41e-cc5fd38caed1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0ce2375f-f324-5d66-88d2-48bdd2d9b48a" :question/math-academy-id "q-132198" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $Y∼\\text{Exp}(\\pi ),$ calculate $P(1\\le Y\\le 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $Y$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda y}, & y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nY∼\\text{Exp}(\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSo, $Y$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\pi {e}^{-\\pi y}, & y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(1\\le Y\\le 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le Y\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\pi {e}^{-\\pi y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\pi y}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3\\pi }+{e}^{-\\pi } \\\\  & ≈0.0431\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590757 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f9c704e-877c-5e19-a553-71eaa0db23b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6045" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590337} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f15f5b-2edc-51cf-9820-892edb82ffd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6065" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590475} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d29bbc-3676-5afd-8efd-bd666bfd90b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6565" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590491} {:answer/id #uuid "d8022a2c-701e-5a46-bd27-6bc97c855e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6605" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590558} {:answer/id #uuid "e940a86f-7435-5a97-9ecd-47f0bad60632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6156" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590591}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590475} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e8cf8bc-9194-5649-8709-cd4b56704e2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590697}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "11d6e15a-f482-5ee9-a082-96558ce44e34" :question/math-academy-id "q-132187" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right),$ calculate $P(X>3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-x/6}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{-x/6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-{e}^{-x/6}|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-1/2} \\\\  & ≈0.6065\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590769 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a77678-46c9-5db7-8ec9-582308885b10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7364" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590250} {:answer/id #uuid "2c0d07df-abc3-544b-b73d-a540c62b65df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6321" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590265} {:answer/id #uuid "464ada53-9a54-5fe5-99a4-666ebdee8d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9502" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590314} {:answer/id #uuid "64b8a84c-8529-50eb-8d85-32629e1d5c9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4866" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590360} {:answer/id #uuid "e546fc4a-0364-5cd9-a9c9-f7956ef026a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590582}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590250} :answer-field/id #uuid "bad16b3f-05f9-5cdf-b44d-ca689361f341" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3aa38dfc-ed32-536a-9b6a-6cebc1f209fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-96404" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right),$ calculate $P(X<2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2x/3}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x/3}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-4/3}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.7364\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590785 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "074c9807-829a-5b98-88e6-e22b5c45096c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0302" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590199} {:answer/id #uuid "999a539f-f5b2-53fc-a3fb-1af00d3d0570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0498" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590442} {:answer/id #uuid "da8ed7c8-7b2e-51c0-b7e1-c140e9888c0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0137" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590566} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f0e059-8023-5f53-9e34-f9efa6044496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0357" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590588} {:answer/id #uuid "ed196434-71ad-5223-ab71-d1bb4bae5e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590604}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590604} :answer-field/id #uuid "b945a8a9-ed36-5138-8d61-d35f93f2715b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "59d51f6d-7542-584a-991a-8702a2c9bfeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-96414" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right),$ calculate $P(X>11).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>11)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>11) & ={\\int }_{11}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{11}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/3}{|}_{11}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-11/3} \\\\  & ≈0.0256\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eadaea8-e7b3-5686-b233-7b20ab0a3079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1937" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590207} {:answer/id #uuid "26d24e13-8cc0-54e2-856a-ff9c409d1e4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1873" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590254} {:answer/id #uuid "74443e3f-bd90-55e0-a6f9-fdc76edc60e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1337" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590382} {:answer/id #uuid "81a5de1b-481c-5f2a-838a-35febcc380e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1984" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590399} {:answer/id #uuid "c95d8814-e1a3-54ed-b4b5-0af395479ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2077" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590524}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590207} :answer-field/id #uuid "47583c9c-029f-521c-88ed-ca428d7df852" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6bef3467-0f78-59bc-8533-35b28f402887" :question/math-academy-id "q-132205" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(0.8),$ calculate $P(2<X\\le 6).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(0.8).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.8{e}^{-0.8x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(2<X\\le 6)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 6) & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}0.8{e}^{-0.8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-0.8x}{|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-4.8}+{e}^{-1.6} \\\\  & ≈0.1937\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fca2e6b-c0fc-54c6-9103-fd7806a0e109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1170" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590274} {:answer/id #uuid "68f0b13b-980e-5bb4-acd7-2d4c2d01155e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0855" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590365} {:answer/id #uuid "711f2c0f-8d35-51b8-94f7-dd4a0f26ea8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0752" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590377} {:answer/id #uuid "bea4ce14-e185-5a34-94b3-e751f9e3d1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3496" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590509} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd3fa9a-2f69-5233-a209-14a8b6a969cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3181" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590531}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590365} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7ccc5a-cc8b-5ab2-a236-f33a76c70d7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "72f86263-9eea-5221-aa9c-3f767d46f4f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96424" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(4),$ calculate $P(\\frac{1}{2}<X<\\frac{3}{4}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(4).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{-4x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(\\frac{1}{2}<X<\\frac{3}{4})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{2}<X<\\frac{3}{4}) & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{3/4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{3/4}4{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-4x}{|}_{1/2}^{3/4} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3}+{e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.0855\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590802 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b0a7bd6-03ae-521b-8545-da3409ed32e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1632" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590223} {:answer/id #uuid "67f667e5-803c-5376-a9ee-3af7b687988d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590363} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c07159-94df-5828-b804-d2d556907b46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1687" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590494} {:answer/id #uuid "b9abd58d-85f0-57dd-ba01-ff9802c19c07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1286" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590503} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ea624a-e6c2-5c01-b9ac-491a50134fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1485" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590585}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218659