/value "0.0695" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590286} {:answer/id #uuid "6e769c95-2f53-5f81-8222-95ee86476ead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3247" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590374} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8eca74-3a05-52dd-872d-76e8d29c4900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1653" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590447}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590286} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac82ac44-2beb-5312-9990-f7e4896d2d61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cb3c3164-617a-5f99-ba4a-1abb3fe0842e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96409" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $Y∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right),$ calculate $P(Y\\ge 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $Y$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda y}, & y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nY∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $Y$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-4y/3}, & y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(Y\\ge 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\ge 2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-4y/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-4y/3}|}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-8/3} \\\\  & ≈0.0695\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186590819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f7f74bb-4b00-544c-bc07-21bf4387972c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4668" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186590299} {:answer/id #uuid "47f9585d-8dab-547c-aa0f-4df65652a7cf" :answe